course: dictionary
lesson: 7247
title: One word, many pictures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word picture can mean different things, and the words around it show you which meaning is right. A picture can be a drawing, a painting or a photo. «Some pictures, like the duck-rabbit, can be seen in two ways.» The clue is that you can see two animals in the same lines, so picture means a drawing.
explain: Picture can also be a verb, which means to see something in your mind. Think about the sentence «Can you picture the beach?» Picture is an action here, not a thing you can hold. Ask yourself: is it a thing or something I do? That question tells you the job the word is doing.
explain: Sometimes picture means the general idea of a situation, as in «get the picture». When you understand what is going on, you have got the picture. Read the whole sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: A picture is a drawing, painting or photo.
fact: To picture something means to see it in your mind, to imagine it.
fact: «Get the picture» means you understand the general idea of a situation.
fact: In maths, a picture graph, also called a pictogram, uses pictures to show numbers.
fact: In old use, «the pictures» means the cinema.
exercise: «Some pictures, like the duck-rabbit, can be seen in two ways.» What is a picture in this sentence? | *A drawing | A kind of sleep | A sum with numbers | A long walk
exercise: «Animation is lots of still pictures, each a tiny bit different, shown very fast.» What are the still pictures? | *Still images, such as drawings or photos | Movements of the body | Lists of numbers | Pieces of music
exercise: In maths, a picture graph uses pictures to show what? | The weather | Words for stories | *Numbers | Colours only
test: «Can you picture the beach?» What does picture mean here? | To paint the walls | To take a photo of it | *To see it in your mind | To measure the sand
test: What does «get the picture» mean? | You buy a picture frame | You draw very fast | *You understand the general idea | You take a photo quickly
exam: Which sentence uses picture as a verb? | *«Can you picture the sea at night?» | «The picture book had lots of dragons.» | «She hung the picture in the hall.» | «The picture was painted by Sam.»
